.TH EITAAS 1 "August 2026" "EITaaS-Linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
eitaas \- diagnose and launch community AVD connections with smart-card redirection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eitaas doctor
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas inspect-profile
.I FILE
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas smartcard status
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas connect
.RI [ FILE ]
.br
.B eitaas profile import
.I FILE
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas profile list
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas profile select
.I NAME
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas profile remove
.I NAME
.br
.B eitaas certificates
.RI { fetch | inspect }
.SH DESCRIPTION
EITaaS-Linux is an independent community helper for diagnosing and launching
Azure Virtual Desktop connections through the bundled one-shot
.BR eitaas-remmina (1)
client, an isolated Remmina and FreeRDP pair installed under a private prefix.
.PP
.B eitaas connect
validates the profile (regular file, owned by the caller, mode 0600, at most
1 MiB, .rdpw extension) and then runs
.B eitaas-remmina FILE
with no other arguments, no shell, and no inherited standard streams. Without
.I FILE
it uses the default profile from the private store (see PROFILE STORE) and
fails with "no imported profile; run: eitaas profile import FILE.rdpw" when
none has been imported. It does not construct RDP or authentication
arguments; all connection policy is applied inside the bundled client.
.PP
.B eitaas profile
manages the private store of imported profiles.
.B import
moves a downloaded .rdpw into the store, restricts it, and makes it the
default;
.B list
prints the stored profiles (names only);
.B select
makes an imported profile the default;
.B remove
deletes it from the store.
.PP
It does not disable certificate verification, request a CAC PIN, or install
polkit rules or certificate trust anchors during ordinary operation.
.SH SECURITY
Connection profiles must be regular files owned by the current user without
group or other permissions. Use chmod 600 on a downloaded profile before use.
.PP
Clipboard redirection has no switch in
.BR eitaas .
The bundled client follows the profile's
.B redirectclipboard
field through Remmina's RDPW importer; a profile that omits the field gets the
RDP default (enabled). This is by design: the exported profile is the policy
source, and the launcher does not override it. The field is not forwarded to
FreeRDP's native profile parser.
.PP
Never publish real RDP/RDPW files or authentication callback URLs. See the
installed SECURITY.md documentation for reporting guidance.
.PP
Authentication uses either the Microsoft Identity Broker (when the bundle was
built with SSO-MIB) or the embedded CAC WebView; the terminal URL/callback
fallback is refused inside the bundled client.
.SH DOCTOR
.B eitaas doctor
reports whether
.B eitaas-remmina
is on PATH, whether the private client binary exists under
.I /usr/libexec/eitaas-remmina
or
.IR /usr/lib/eitaas-remmina ,
the pinned Remmina and FreeRDP versions from the installed
.I sources.json
manifest (or "unknown"), whether the installed FreeRDP client library links
SSO-MIB, identity-broker registration on the session bus, the PC/SC socket,
and the presence of smart-card tools. Readiness requires the launcher, the
private client, and healthy smart-card checks. The report also names the
newest session log written by
.B eitaas connect
as
.BR latest_session_log .
.SH SESSION LOGS
Every connection writes the client's standard output and error, redacted
line by line, to
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/eitaas-remmina/logs/session-TIMESTAMP-PID.log
(default
.IR ~/.local/state/eitaas-remmina/logs/ ;
directory mode 0700, files mode 0600, about 2 MiB each, the newest five
kept). The first lines record the helper version, the profile basename, and
the number of
.B remmina
processes already running; the last line is
.BR exit=CODE .
The bundled client logs each smart-card authentication stage as
.BR "smartcard-auth: CODE" .
The codes are stable: challenge-received, challenge-accepted,
origin-rejected, discovery-start, discovery-token-skipped-trust,
discovery-token-empty, discovery-finished, discovery-busy, discovery-empty,
discovery-timeout, discovery-error, discovery-cancelled,
discovery-result-discarded, certificate-selected, certificate-submitted,
selection-cancelled, load-start, load-finished, load-timeout, load-error,
load-cancelled, load-result-discarded, pin-requested, pin-submitted,
pin-rejected, pin-cancelled, and oneshot-quit; the README lists the
parameters of each. Every dialog the client shows is logged at warning level
with the same code. The launcher enables the
.B remmina
debug domain (G_MESSAGES_DEBUG) so these lines reach the session log and a
terminal; Remmina additionally appends its debug output to
.IR $TMPDIR/remmina_log_file.log .
The "remmina instances already running" header counts every process named
.B remmina
(any Remmina binary, not only the bundled one). Certificate labels, PKCS #11
URIs, PINs, and tokens are never logged.
.SH PROFILE STORE
.B eitaas profile import
requires a regular .rdpw file owned by the caller, at most 1 MiB, not a
symbolic link, and not already in the store. The file is moved (renamed, or
copied with fsync and unlinked across filesystems) into
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/eitaas-remmina/profiles/
(default
.IR ~/.local/share/eitaas-remmina/profiles/ ),
which is created with mode 0700 and must be owned by the caller. The stored
file keeps its basename (a -2, -3, ... suffix is added on collision) and is
set to mode 0600.
.PP
The default name is written to
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/eitaas/profiles.ini
(default
.IR ~/.config/eitaas/profiles.ini ,
mode 0600) as the only key:
.B [profiles] default = NAME.
When the configured name no longer exists, or the file is absent, the most
recently imported profile is the default. Removing the default profile makes
the next most recent import the default.
.PP
Profile contents are never parsed by the store; listings show the basename,
cloud classification, size, mode, and import time only. Errors use the codes
.B profile_import_failed
and
.BR profile_store_failed .
The graphical helper
.BR eitaas-gui (1)
uses the same store.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. One indicates completed diagnostics with unmet
requirements. Two indicates invalid input or an operation error. A connection
otherwise returns the exit status of the
.B eitaas-remmina
child.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR eitaas-gui (1),
.BR pcsc_scan (1),
.BR pkcs11-tool (1),
.BR remmina (1)
